    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The 1215 charter failed as a peace treaty within months, but its reissues from 1216 onwards embedded it in English political life.</li><li>From the late 16th century lawyers such as Sir Edward Coke read it as the restoration of an ancient English constitution, an account modern historians call a myth.</li><li>The charter concerned the relations between the king and the barons, yet it shaped ideas of due process and influenced the founders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Only three clauses of Magna Carta remain on the statute book of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>: the freedom of the English Church, the ancient liberties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">City of London</a> and the right to due legal process.</p></aside>
    </section>

